1
00:00:15,180 --> 00:00:16,897
Destiny. Fate. Dreams.

2
00:00:16,980 --> 00:00:21,140
These unstoppable ideals are
held deep in the heart of man.

3
00:00:21,540 --> 00:00:24,937
As long as there are people
who seek freedom in this life,

4
00:00:25,020 --> 00:00:27,667
these things shall not
vanish from the earth.

5
00:00:34,680 --> 00:00:37,497
People tell me my head's in the clouds.

6
00:00:37,580 --> 00:00:40,897
I don't care what they say
because I'm dreaming of you.

7
00:00:40,980 --> 00:00:43,557
You are the treasure I found.

8
00:00:43,640 --> 00:00:46,657
So bright, so bold, and so elusive.

9
00:00:46,740 --> 00:00:48,717
It's hard to look away.

10
00:00:48,800 --> 00:00:51,857
Even though it's blinding me.

11
00:00:51,940 --> 00:00:55,657
There are no words to
describe how I feel inside.

12
00:00:55,740 --> 00:00:58,020
I'm really, really stuck on you.

13
00:00:59,200 --> 00:01:02,537
I have to follow my dreams,
however crazy they seem.

14
00:01:02,620 --> 00:01:05,577
And I won't stop till I
get there, you will see.

15
00:01:05,660 --> 00:01:08,877
You're all I need to have
the strength to believe.

16
00:01:08,960 --> 00:01:12,120
We live in wonderland.

17
00:01:17,900 --> 00:01:21,117
I'm gonna follow my dreams,
however crazy they seem.

18
00:01:21,200 --> 00:01:24,157
I'm gonna share them
with you, a love so true.

19
00:01:24,240 --> 00:01:27,557
You're all I want,
together we can move on.

20
00:01:27,640 --> 00:01:29,917
We live how we want to.

21
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:32,037
There is no limit to us.

22
00:01:32,120 --> 00:01:33,537
We have the power of love.

23
00:01:33,620 --> 00:01:36,637
We don't want to live ordinary lives.

24
00:01:36,720 --> 00:01:39,757
We have a chance to live in paradise.

25
00:01:39,840 --> 00:01:42,500
We live in one another.

26
00:02:08,660 --> 00:02:10,080
What's the matter?

27
00:02:12,360 --> 00:02:13,860
It's fine.

28
00:02:53,480 --> 00:02:54,960
Oh, my God.

29
00:03:05,120 --> 00:03:05,950
He...

30
00:03:06,033 --> 00:03:07,317
he blocked that hit with his helmet!

31
00:03:07,400 --> 00:03:08,230
That's incredible!

32
00:03:08,313 --> 00:03:11,751
A couple of inches left to ride
and it would've killed him!

33
00:03:26,740 --> 00:03:28,580
What an incredible fight, huh?

34
00:03:29,280 --> 00:03:32,197
Every one of those attacks
is aimed at some vital spot.

35
00:03:32,280 --> 00:03:34,397
Just one slip from either
of them and that's it.

36
00:03:34,480 --> 00:03:35,310
They're dead.

37
00:03:35,393 --> 00:03:38,757
These guys have really been
fighting to the death for 100 years?

38
00:03:38,840 --> 00:03:40,134
That's got to get old.

39
00:03:41,440 --> 00:03:42,740
This is a good thing.

40
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:45,700
This is our chance to get away. Let's go.

41
00:03:56,440 --> 00:03:57,270
Usopp?

42
00:04:00,500 --> 00:04:01,330
Amazing.

43
00:04:03,820 --> 00:04:04,650
Why?

44
00:04:05,480 --> 00:04:06,820
I don't remember.

45
00:04:13,900 --> 00:04:17,560
They fight so seriously, and
they don't even know why.

46
00:04:19,520 --> 00:04:21,696
This fight's getting really annoying.

47
00:04:21,780 --> 00:04:22,610
Don't you see?

48
00:04:22,900 --> 00:04:26,380
This is an example of a real
battle between real men.

49
00:04:27,660 --> 00:04:28,490
Hmm?

50
00:04:28,573 --> 00:04:29,403
Say what?

51
00:04:29,620 --> 00:04:31,240
Maybe an analogy will help.

52
00:04:31,480 --> 00:04:35,957
It's as if they have each planted a flag
in their hearts that says, I am a warrior.

53
00:04:36,040 --> 00:04:40,158
This flag is more important than
anything, more than their lives even.

54
00:04:41,040 --> 00:04:44,317
They can never allow the flag
to be destroyed by someone else.

55
00:04:44,400 --> 00:04:47,988
That's why they both continue
this fight for a hundred years.

56
00:04:51,060 --> 00:04:52,400
Do you see it now?

57
00:04:52,780 --> 00:04:54,420
This is a proud duel.

58
00:04:54,720 --> 00:04:58,520
A legendary fight between
two dedicated warriors.

59
00:04:59,860 --> 00:05:00,860
Yeah, whatever.

60
00:05:01,140 --> 00:05:03,757
That warrior stuff doesn't really
interest me in the slightest.

61
00:05:03,840 --> 00:05:04,670
You coming.

62
00:05:04,820 --> 00:05:06,800
No, I'm still watching this.

63
00:05:09,180 --> 00:05:10,637
This is my ultimate goal.

64
00:05:10,720 --> 00:05:11,757
This right here.

65
00:05:11,840 --> 00:05:14,664
To be a brave warrior
like each of these titans.

66
00:05:15,200 --> 00:05:16,237
Really though, someday.

67
00:05:16,320 --> 00:05:18,560
I will be a proud warrior of the sea.

68
00:05:25,300 --> 00:05:26,937
So what you're saying then?

69
00:05:27,020 --> 00:05:28,844
Is that you want to be a giant?

70
00:05:30,340 --> 00:05:31,170
Moron!

71
00:05:31,253 --> 00:05:33,197
You haven't listened to a
single word I've said, have you?

72
00:05:33,280 --> 00:05:37,339
Hey, Usopp Isn't there something
that you're supposed to be watching?

73
00:05:41,900 --> 00:05:44,557
If there's a village full
of warriors like these two,

74
00:05:44,640 --> 00:05:46,934
then I really want to go there someday.

75
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:06,000
It's safe to say that we're both
starting to get homesick here.

76
00:06:08,920 --> 00:06:09,750
Ah, Dory.

77
00:06:09,833 --> 00:06:12,327
That's why I intend to
win this duel of ours.

78
00:06:12,520 --> 00:06:14,757
I'm going to beat you
and go home to Elbath.

79
00:06:14,840 --> 00:06:16,020
Got that, Broggy?

80
00:06:31,740 --> 00:06:35,340
73,466 duels.

81
00:06:35,540 --> 00:06:39,740
73,466 duels.

82
00:07:06,680 --> 00:07:10,240
Hey, if you're done, get out of the way.

83
00:07:12,240 --> 00:07:14,360
Wait, I can handle this.

84
00:07:16,800 --> 00:07:18,880
3,000 telegram press!

85
00:07:31,840 --> 00:07:33,720
Oh, hello, Mr. Five.

86
00:07:36,020 --> 00:07:37,577
I'm impressed by the decor.

87
00:07:37,660 --> 00:07:40,977
You have a talent for turning even the
most savage environment into a home.

88
00:07:41,060 --> 00:07:44,057
I admire you, which is why I feel
compelled to remind both of you.

89
00:07:44,140 --> 00:07:46,217
This mission belongs to
me and Miss Valentine.

90
00:07:46,300 --> 00:07:49,537
Rest assured, we won't slip
up like we did last time.

91
00:07:49,620 --> 00:07:50,450
Slip up?

92
00:07:50,533 --> 00:07:54,357
That's not why I'm here,
Mr Five, Miss Valentine.

93
00:07:54,440 --> 00:07:56,997
The simple fact of the
matter is you are both weak.

94
00:07:57,080 --> 00:08:02,097
Don't waste your energy pouting.

95
00:08:02,180 --> 00:08:03,277
It is what it is.

96
00:08:03,360 --> 00:08:04,837
Take a look at this.

97
00:08:04,920 --> 00:08:09,717
I'd like to thank you both for affording
me an excuse to come to this island.

98
00:08:09,800 --> 00:08:11,637
I'll enjoy the opportunity to hunt.

99
00:08:11,720 --> 00:08:13,960
some truly big game.

100
00:08:15,820 --> 00:08:20,055
Dory the Blue Ogre and Brogy the Red
Ogre are the giant warrior pirates.

101
00:08:20,940 --> 00:08:22,057
Everyone's heard of them.

102
00:08:22,140 --> 00:08:23,117
It's ancient legend.

103
00:08:23,200 --> 00:08:25,435
Hey, this poster's over 100 years old.

104
00:08:25,560 --> 00:08:28,917
Well, those two legends are alive
and well on this very island,

105
00:08:29,000 --> 00:08:30,647
battling over a century now.

106
00:08:31,040 --> 00:08:32,397
Back when that poster was new,

107
00:08:32,480 --> 00:08:35,337
the bounty on their heads was
100 million berries apiece,

108
00:08:35,420 --> 00:08:37,337
200 million for the both of them.

109
00:08:37,420 --> 00:08:39,797
200 million berries is an impressive sum.

110
00:08:39,880 --> 00:08:41,837
but that doesn't change the
fact that they're giants

111
00:08:41,920 --> 00:08:44,877
there's a wise saying
superior criminals are those

112
00:08:44,960 --> 00:08:47,417
who execute their crimes
using superior intellect

113
00:08:47,500 --> 00:08:50,620
all you have to do is follow
my precise instructions

114
00:08:51,120 --> 00:08:53,497
with a smidgen of forethought
and perseverance you

115
00:08:53,580 --> 00:08:56,698
can find the solution to
even the most gargantuan of?

116
00:09:06,860 --> 00:09:07,801
...of obstacles.

117
00:09:21,060 --> 00:09:24,531
Hey, Dory, a couple of guests
of mine gave me some alcohol.

118
00:09:25,020 --> 00:09:25,850
Drinks?

119
00:09:26,060 --> 00:09:27,600
It's been a long while.

120
00:09:27,780 --> 00:09:28,640
Hey, Brogy?

121
00:09:37,780 --> 00:09:38,898
That's interesting.

122
00:09:39,020 --> 00:09:41,337
So Bragi's guests are
friends of yours, then.

123
00:09:41,420 --> 00:09:44,897
I saw a goofy-looking guy with
a long nose and a woman there.

124
00:09:44,980 --> 00:09:46,280
That's Usopp and Nami.

125
00:09:46,480 --> 00:09:48,557
They said they weren't even
gonna get off the ship.

126
00:09:48,640 --> 00:09:51,357
I guess they wanted to have
an adventure after all.

127
00:09:51,440 --> 00:09:53,697
If they're your friends,
then I guess I can thank you,

128
00:09:53,780 --> 00:09:55,780
too, for these yummy refreshments.

129
00:09:58,200 --> 00:10:03,024
So, Dory, tell us, does it really take a
year for the log to reset on this island?

130
00:10:03,380 --> 00:10:04,210
Yes.

131
00:10:04,293 --> 00:10:07,737
You notice all the mounds of human
skeletons that are lying around here?

132
00:10:07,820 --> 00:10:09,291
I guess it's hard not to.

133
00:10:10,080 --> 00:10:14,017
The people who come to this island tend
to die before their logs are reset.

134
00:10:14,100 --> 00:10:15,820
Some become dinosaur food.

135
00:10:16,080 --> 00:10:18,840
Some die from heat or
thirst or starvation.

136
00:10:19,580 --> 00:10:22,137
Others are killed because
they stupidly attack us.

137
00:10:22,220 --> 00:10:24,867
Whatever the case, they
all die here somehow.

138
00:10:25,940 --> 00:10:29,157
An entire year on this island
just seems to be too long.

139
00:10:29,240 --> 00:10:32,717
So far, no humans have been able
to survive here for the full year.

140
00:10:32,800 --> 00:10:34,212
What are we going to do?

141
00:10:34,420 --> 00:10:37,177
Even if we could manage
to last here for a year,

142
00:10:37,260 --> 00:10:39,097
who knows what could happen by then?

143
00:10:39,180 --> 00:10:40,651
My country could be lost.

144
00:10:41,700 --> 00:10:42,620
She's right.

145
00:10:43,020 --> 00:10:45,138
Plus, I get bored here after a year.

146
00:10:45,500 --> 00:10:48,517
Isn't there anything else
we can do about it, old man?

147
00:10:48,600 --> 00:10:49,430
Hmm.

148
00:10:49,513 --> 00:10:51,020
We do have an eternal pose here,

149
00:10:51,180 --> 00:10:54,237
but its magnetic link is to
our home village, Elbath.

150
00:10:54,320 --> 00:10:55,150
Basically,

151
00:10:55,233 --> 00:10:56,797
that eternal pose is
what Broggy and I have

152
00:10:56,880 --> 00:10:59,762
been fighting for with
our duels this whole time.

153
00:11:00,000 --> 00:11:02,700
Of course, you can try
to take it by force.

154
00:11:02,860 --> 00:11:04,389
No, that's not gonna work.

155
00:11:04,500 --> 00:11:06,797
Elbaf isn't the place that
we're trying to get to.

156
00:11:06,880 --> 00:11:10,377
We just want to get to the island
that's right after this one, right?

157
00:11:10,460 --> 00:11:11,290
Yes.

158
00:11:11,860 --> 00:11:14,797
We must stay on the route that's
going to lead us to my home,

159
00:11:14,880 --> 00:11:16,351
or else there's no point.

160
00:11:16,600 --> 00:11:17,430
Yeah.

161
00:11:18,940 --> 00:11:21,397
Maybe you can try
sailing forward randomly.

162
00:11:21,480 --> 00:11:23,186
You may get there eventually.

163
00:11:23,560 --> 00:11:24,795
If you're real lucky.

164
00:11:32,740 --> 00:11:33,740
Maybe so.

165
00:11:36,420 --> 00:11:38,560
We may actually get there.

166
00:11:42,240 --> 00:11:43,780
Now that I think about it,

167
00:11:43,900 --> 00:11:46,857
someone did leave the island
once before his log was reset.

168
00:11:46,940 --> 00:11:48,357
And what happened to him?

169
00:11:48,440 --> 00:11:49,860
How should I know that?

170
00:11:50,040 --> 00:11:52,497
I'm sure he was able to
get to the next island.

171
00:11:52,580 --> 00:11:53,840
That must be it.

172
00:11:57,820 --> 00:11:59,440
What is so funny?

173
00:12:06,520 --> 00:12:11,226
I don't understand what these two idiots
are laughing about at a time like this.

174
00:12:16,560 --> 00:12:18,920
A brave warrior of the seas, you said.

175
00:12:19,200 --> 00:12:20,460
What's that exactly?

176
00:12:20,760 --> 00:12:22,420
I'm talking about you guys.

177
00:12:22,580 --> 00:12:25,933
What I really want is to be
like the two of you some day.

178
00:12:26,100 --> 00:12:26,930
Huh?

179
00:12:27,013 --> 00:12:27,880
You want to be a giant?

180
00:12:28,300 --> 00:12:29,240
You hear that?

181
00:12:29,360 --> 00:12:30,713
That's not what I mean!

182
00:12:31,600 --> 00:12:33,306
I want to be a great warrior.

183
00:12:33,580 --> 00:12:37,404
I want to be brave and proud like
you and the others from Elbath.

184
00:12:41,100 --> 00:12:41,980
I see.

185
00:12:42,660 --> 00:12:46,457
You know, in Elbath, even though our
lifespans are longer than yours are,

186
00:12:46,540 --> 00:12:48,716
we still think about how we will die.

187
00:12:49,320 --> 00:12:53,940
We know everything we have and everything
we are will one day cease to exist,

188
00:12:54,140 --> 00:12:55,277
like everything else.

189
00:12:55,360 --> 00:13:00,197
But it is worth it to die a true warrior
of Elbath, without sacrificing your pride.

190
00:13:00,280 --> 00:13:02,515
That is what we call dying with honor.

191
00:13:02,800 --> 00:13:06,271
To die such a great death would
be an everlasting treasure.

192
00:13:06,520 --> 00:13:08,180
It's what we seek in Elbath.

193
00:13:09,300 --> 00:13:11,020
So pride is your treasure.

194
00:13:11,420 --> 00:13:12,380
That's great.

195
00:13:12,780 --> 00:13:14,597
I've decided to learn from you.

196
00:13:14,680 --> 00:13:16,897
From now on, I'll call you Master.

197
00:13:16,980 --> 00:13:17,840
Huh?

198
00:13:36,120 --> 00:13:37,580
Oh, giant guy!

199
00:13:40,280 --> 00:13:41,640
What's going on?

200
00:13:41,880 --> 00:13:43,260
Why did it explode?

201
00:13:43,620 --> 00:13:46,417
That was the same alcohol
we had with us on the ship,

202
00:13:46,500 --> 00:13:52,017
wasn't it it exploded in his stomach the

203
00:13:52,100 --> 00:13:54,335
other giant must have booby-trapped it

204
00:13:55,440 --> 00:13:58,237
hold it were you even watching them they

205
00:13:58,320 --> 00:14:01,240
fight their duels honorably
no way he'd do that

206
00:14:02,700 --> 00:14:04,620
all right then who did do it

207
00:14:07,700 --> 00:14:08,980
You strangers!

208
00:14:11,280 --> 00:14:13,120
That wasn't Froggy!

209
00:14:14,780 --> 00:14:15,860
No way!

210
00:14:16,700 --> 00:14:19,100
No warrior of Elbaf would dare!

211
00:14:19,460 --> 00:14:22,840
So, who else is there to
suspect on this island then?

212
00:14:23,340 --> 00:14:24,500
Besides you!

213
00:14:26,200 --> 00:14:27,500
Let's get out of here!

214
00:14:27,700 --> 00:14:29,777
There's no use talking to him right now!

215
00:14:29,860 --> 00:14:31,837
I doubt running would do us any good.

216
00:14:31,920 --> 00:14:34,020
Hold on to this! Stay back!

217
00:14:35,020 --> 00:14:36,757
You're going to...

218
00:14:36,840 --> 00:14:37,980
fight Dory?

219
00:14:41,340 --> 00:14:42,860
Yeah, I don't want to.

220
00:14:43,260 --> 00:14:44,848
But we have to settle this.

221
00:14:49,820 --> 00:14:52,300
Don't do it, you guys! Stop it!

222
00:14:52,780 --> 00:14:54,604
Dory, please just listen to me!

223
00:14:54,720 --> 00:14:57,877
We don't know anything about the
explosives in the barrels, I promise!

224
00:14:57,960 --> 00:14:59,017
We wouldn't do that!

225
00:14:59,100 --> 00:15:02,688
You can't be in any shape to
fight right now, so please stop!

226
00:15:05,160 --> 00:15:05,990
Right.

227
00:15:06,073 --> 00:15:09,020
Why should I believe you liars?

228
00:15:20,620 --> 00:15:22,780
All right then, Gum-Gum!

229
00:15:40,880 --> 00:15:42,280
GUNGUNFUL!

230
00:15:50,340 --> 00:15:51,740
GUNGUNFUL!

231
00:15:52,440 --> 00:15:53,757
Sorry…

232
00:15:53,840 --> 00:15:54,800
BROCKER!

233
00:16:24,080 --> 00:16:25,640
No! Luffy!

234
00:16:25,980 --> 00:16:30,500
He has some power from
one of the devil fruits.

235
00:16:31,840 --> 00:16:37,620
It seems I underestimated him.

236
00:16:55,800 --> 00:17:01,277
Luffy are you all right how is he he

237
00:17:01,360 --> 00:17:03,637
should be okay i guess you were right

238
00:17:03,720 --> 00:17:05,577
about fighting He's certainly a lot

239
00:17:05,660 --> 00:17:12,057
calmer now well i'm not the old guy was

240
00:17:12,140 --> 00:17:15,657
right about one thing anyway The other
giant would never do anything like

241
00:17:15,740 --> 00:17:20,269
this but i know that our friends wouldn't
do it either They aren't like that.

242
00:17:20,840 --> 00:17:22,600
Yeah, then who?

243
00:17:23,000 --> 00:17:25,540
There must be somebody
else on this island.

244
00:17:34,060 --> 00:17:38,119
The key to winning any game is to
know your opponent's state of mind.

245
00:17:38,320 --> 00:17:41,202
For now we have succeeded
in confusing our enemy.

246
00:17:41,300 --> 00:17:44,917
They are no doubt wondering about the
mysterious bomb that we delivered.

247
00:17:45,000 --> 00:17:47,824
And about the identity
of their invisible enemy.

248
00:17:49,040 --> 00:17:52,140
Our first target was the
long-bearded giant Dory.

249
00:17:52,440 --> 00:17:55,837
I knew, of course, that it would be
nearly impossible to finish him off,

250
00:17:55,920 --> 00:18:00,297
but the damage done to his stomach by
the bomb must have been considerable.

251
00:18:00,380 --> 00:18:01,210
Now,

252
00:18:01,293 --> 00:18:06,180
we can sit here enjoying our tea while
relaxing and wait for the next duel to start.

253
00:18:07,140 --> 00:18:11,375
So we stay in the background and let
the giant kill off the injured one?

254
00:18:12,280 --> 00:18:13,920
Yes, that's exactly right.

255
00:18:14,420 --> 00:18:16,377
That's certainly an indirect method.

256
00:18:16,460 --> 00:18:18,597
Again, you have to consider your enemy.

